argRoundJ -- argRoundT's JIT arm, IN ITS OWN FILE.

Two files because a fixture gets ONE testing(): a second call on the same
action hits the sequential-state-corruption tar baby, and bear-trap #25 says
an interpreted run first consumes isCoded and silently reroutes testing() to
jitRunIfTest. So the interpreted oracle lives in argRoundT and the jitted arm
lives here, and neither can spoil the other.

⚠ THIS FILE IS PINNED TO A KNOWN DEFECT AND IS EXPECTED TO BE WRONG.
jitArgBake: where the JIT gives a callee its OWN FUNCTION rather than inlining
it, the callee's `argument` is read from an address baked at emit time and does
not track the run-time bind. So the argument column here prints ADDRESSES where
argRoundT's interpreted column prints 7.

    interpreted (argRoundT)   argument = 7 at every depth       CORRECT
    jitted      (this file)   argument = a large number          THE DEFECT

⚠ THE LOCAL COLUMN AGREES ON BOTH ENGINES -- 3/2/1 -- and that is what makes
this a statement about the ARGUMENT CHANNEL rather than about the frame. A
fixture that only showed the jitted side would not be able to say which.

WHEN jitArgBake LANDS this file starts printing 7 and its pop.sh row goes RED.
That is the signal, not a regression: re-pin the row to 7 with a sentence
(rule H6 -- a parked pin that starts passing must graduate, and a re-pin needs
a cause, not a green diff).
